/**
 * Florida Value Adjustment Board (VAB) Clerk mailing addresses — all 67 counties.
 *
 * WHY THIS FILE EXISTS:
 * A DR-486 petition and its filing-fee check must be mailed to the CLERK OF THE
 * VALUE ADJUSTMENT BOARD — *not* to the county Property Appraiser. Mailing to the
 * Property Appraiser means the petition is never filed and the customer loses the
 * appeal year. Before this file existed, the destination address was generated by
 * an LLM at request time and cached in Redis for 180 days, unvalidated. That is
 * never acceptable for addressing government mail. This table is the single source
 * of truth and the filing path must not fall back to any other source.
 *
 * DO NOT GUESS. If a county is not `confirmed` below, orders for that county are
 * blocked at checkout (see isFlCountySupported). A blocked sale is recoverable;
 * a misdelivered petition is not.
 *
 * NOTE — non-obvious VAB clerks (these are NOT the Clerk of the Circuit Court):
 *   Orange   → Orange County Comptroller
 *   Duval    → City of Jacksonville, City Hall
 *   Broward  → County VAB office, Governmental Center Room 120
 *   Volusia  → County Council administration building
 *   Pasco    → Board Records Division
 *   Pinellas → Board Records Department
 *
 * Researched 2026-07-28 from official county government sources. Each entry
 * carries the sourceUrl it was verified against.
 *
 * REVIEW REMINDER: the 12 `unconfirmed` counties each need one phone call to the
 * VAB clerk to confirm the petition mailing address. Until then they are blocked.
 */

// Counties that require PHYSICAL RECEIPT by the deadline and explicitly state
// that a postmark is NOT sufficient. These need extra lead time before the
